UBI provides a guaranteed income to all citizens, ensuring a baseline to cover basic needs regardless of employment status.
Studies show that UBI can reduce poverty and financial stress, allowing individuals to focus on education, health, and entrepreneurship.
By eliminating means-testing, UBI avoids the administrative burden and stigma associated with traditional welfare programs.
UBI can stimulate local economies by increasing consumer spending, which in turn supports businesses and job creation.
Historical examples, such as Alaska's oil dividend, demonstrate that UBI can be implemented successfully and benefit all members of society.